What will be the output:
```python
class A:
    def __init__(self): print("A")
class B(A):
    def __init__(self):
        print("B") # no super() call
b = B()
```

What will be the output:

```python
class Vehicle:
    def __init__(self, reg): self.reg = reg
class Bike(Vehicle):
    def __init__(self, reg, has_carrier):
        self.has_carrier = has_carrier
b = Bike("KA02", True)
print(b.reg)
```

```python
class A:
    def hook(self): return ["A"]
class B(A):
    def hook(self): return ["B"] + super().hook()
class C(A):
    def hook(self): return ["C"] + super().hook()
class D(B, C):
    def hook(self): return ["D"] + super().hook()
print(D().hook())
```
